<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.5.4: A Quadratic Expression that Represents the Relationship between Distance and Time</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01819</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.5.4: A Quadratic Expression that Represents the Relationship between Distance and Time</md:title>
    <md:uuid>d4103c2b-637b-4b09-9bd8-9047bcd2406b</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>The expression \(16t^2\) represents the distance in feet an object falls after \(t\) seconds. Assume an object is dropped from a height of 906 feet.</para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What is the height of the object in feet 2 seconds after it is dropped?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>The object is at 842 feet 2 seconds after it’s dropped. \(906-16(2)^2=906-16(4)=906-64=842\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Write an expression representing the height of the object in feet \(t\) seconds after it is dropped.</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(906-16t^2\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example></section>
</content>
